{{also|Linggo}}
==Tagalog==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|tl|lingo}} {{q|proscribed, archaic}}
* {{alter|tl|dinggo}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{bor|tl|es|domingo||Sunday}}, which was possibly mistakenly analyzed as {{m|tl|luminggo}} (e.g. ''Luminggo na'', "It's Sunday", which could have been taken to mean "It's been a week"), from which the word is derived by removing the seeming infix {{m|tl|-um-}}.

According to Wolff(1976), it could also be from {{bor|tl|ms|minggu||week}}, which is from {{der|tl|pt|domingo||Sunday}}. Wolff(1976) argues that the change in initial nasal to ⟨l⟩ is also attested for {{cog|tl|langka}} and {{cog|ms|nangka}}.

